    {
      "question": "e-8932",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "80d92c7867ddbc8e5d7dafc168eaf62523586cbc7b4d2c974f40917aa193b860",
      "new_sha256": "b9012762e08029661f720e58bd05ba57aeb0ecc9444cd3e897807da5b23acebb",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8932",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-4 \\\\  & 5{x}^{2}-2x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+11x-13\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20{x}^{2}+11x-13 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,20{x}^{2}+8x-8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $x^2-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $3x-5.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4-2x^3-18x^2+11x-13}{5x^2-2x+2}=x^2-4 + \\dfrac{3x-5}{5x^2-2x+2}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14055203/example-8932.json",
          "file_sha256": "22faa5b4a445a38771b9052681e5dfd9eb3de3d2c484275aa9db40b5aa0a2b57"
