    {
      "question": "e-5144",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "ae954611d31952905c1db1c6dbf75e47f8fe9115c510e44d00252f7661beb166",
      "new_sha256": "92aac664abb358d62d1020d303dc479afae515da423d24f09b1ceac6811a183b",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5144",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^3$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n2x^4-7x^2-x+8 = 2x^4+{\\color{red}0}x^3-7x^2-x+8\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}-x+8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}-x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{2}+0x+5}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is ${2x^2 - 5},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${-x+3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 + \\dfrac{-x+3}{x^2-1}.\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^4 - 7x^2 - x +8}{x^2 - 1} \n= \n2x^2-5 - \\dfrac{x-3}{x^2-1}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14055203/example-5144.json",
          "file_sha256": "5ffe784e3e97829c4ac4a3da76a26fb7bfff337f9de7b4aa5b48bbf6c19d3c8b"
        }
